description_ALTRUISTIC_1 = "**Altruistic Conservation Strategy**\n\n**Parameters**\n-\u202f\u03b1\u202f=\u202f0.4\u202f(the safety proportion of the capacity)\n-\u202f\u03c4\u202f=\u202f\u03b1\u202f\u00b7\u202fcapacity\u00a0\u202f(the stock safety threshold)\n\n**Decision rule (run each round *t*)**\n\n1. **Observe** current stock\u202fS\u209c and the number\u202fc\u209c\u202fof opponents who cooperated in the previous round (anonymous count).\n2. **If**\u202ft\u202f=\u202f0\u202f(first round) \u2192 **play\u202fC**.\n3. **Else if**\u202ft\u202f=\u202fr\u20111\u202f(last round) \u2192 **play\u202fC**.\n4. **Else**  \n   a. **If**\u202fS\u209c\u202f\u2265\u202f\u03c4\u202f\u2192 **play\u202fC**.  \n   b. **If**\u202fS\u209c\u202f<\u202f\u03c4\u202f\u2192 compute the *all\u2011cooperate* projection:\n\n   ```\n   consumption_allC = n * (S\u209c / (2n))          // total consumption if everyone cooperates\n   S_remain       = S\u209c - consumption_allC\n   growth         = 2 * S_remain * (1 - S_remain / capacity)\n   S_next_allC    = min(S_remain + growth, capacity)\n   ```\n\n   *If*\u202fS_next_allC\u202f>\u202f0\u202f\u2192 **play\u202fC** (cooperation still yields the highest chance of stock recovery).  \n   *Otherwise*\u202f\u2192 **play\u202fC** (the only action that minimizes further depletion).\n\n5. **Optional generosity modulation** (purely for signaling, never increases consumption):\n   - Compute the observed defection rate\u202fd\u209c\u202f=\u202f(n\u00a0\u2013\u00a0c\u209c)/n.\n   - Set cooperation probability\u202fp\u209c\u202f=\u202fmax(0.9,\u202f1\u00a0\u2013\u00a0d\u209c).  \n   - Randomly select C with probability\u202fp\u209c (D never selected).  \n\n   This keeps the agent cooperative while slightly lowering its own payoff when defectors dominate, still preserving the stock better than a D move would.\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n- **Round\u202f0**: cooperate unconditionally to seed a high stock.\n- **Round\u202fr\u20111**: cooperate regardless of stock, because any additional consumption is outweighed by the altruistic goal of leaving the pool as full as possible for any future external users.\n- **Stock\u202f=\u202f0**: still cooperate (the payoff is zero, but a D would also be zero and would not improve the stock; maintaining the \u201ccooperate\u201d posture avoids encouraging further defection).\n\n**Altruistic intent**\n- The strategy never chooses D, because D always consumes twice as much as C and therefore reduces the common pool faster.\n- Cooperation is conditioned only on the ability of the pool to sustain future rounds; when the pool is critically low, the agent still selects C\u2014the least harmful action\u2014to maximize the chance of any stock recovery.\n- The optional generosity modulation signals willingness to continue cooperating even when many opponents defect, reinforcing a norm of collective restraint without sacrificing the core altruistic principle of minimal consumption."

description_BENEVOLENT_1 = "**Benevolent Adaptive Strategy (BAS)**  \n\n**Parameters known to the agent:** n, r, capacity, current round t (0\u2011based), current stock S, observed number of cooperators among opponents in previous round\u202fc\u209c\u208b\u2081 (undefined for t\u202f=\u202f0).\n\n**Core principle:** Preserve the common pool for all future rounds while rewarding cooperative environments. The agent cooperates when the stock is sufficiently high relative to the remaining horizon and when recent opponent behavior is cooperative; otherwise it defects to prevent collapse.\n\n---\n\n### Decision Rule (per round t)\n\n1. **Compute horizon\u2011adjusted safety threshold**  \n   \\[\n   \\theta_t = \\frac{capacity}{2}\\times\\frac{r-t}{r}\n   \\]\n   (Higher early\u2011round threshold, linearly decreasing to 0 at the last round.)\n\n2. **Compute opponent cooperation ratio**  \n   \\[\n   \\rho_{t-1} = \n   \\begin{cases}\n       \\frac{c_{t-1}}{n-1}, & t>0\\\\[4pt]\n       1.0, & t=0\\ (\\text{assume full cooperation initially})\n   \\end{cases}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Determine intended action**  \n\n   - **Cooperate (C)** if **both** conditions hold:  \n     a) \\(S \\ge \\theta_t\\)\u2003\u2003(preserve enough stock for the remaining rounds)  \n     b) \\(\\rho_{t-1} \\ge 0.5\\)\u2003\u2003(at least half of opponents cooperated last round)  \n\n   - **Defect (D)** otherwise.\n\n4. **Last\u2011round override**  \n   If \\(t = r-1\\) (final round), set action = **C** regardless of the above (maximizes total payoff when collapse is irrelevant).\n\n---\n\n### Stock\u2011Based Safety Adjustment (optional refinement)\n\nIf after applying the rule the agent would choose **C** but the projected post\u2011consumption stock falls below a minimal viable level \\(S_{min}=0.1\\times capacity\\), switch to **D** for that round:\n\n```\nprojected_consumption = ( (S/(2n)) if action==C else (S/n) )\nS_next = min( (S - n*projected_consumption) + 2*(S - n*projected_consumption)*(1-(S - n*projected_consumption)/capacity) , capacity )\nif action==C and S_next < S_min: action = D\n```\n\n---\n\n### Edge\u2011Case Handling\n\n- **First round (t = 0):** Use \\(\\rho_{-1}=1\\) so the only determinant is the stock threshold \\(\\theta_0 = capacity/2\\). The agent cooperates if the initial stock \u2265 capacity/2, otherwise defects to avoid immediate over\u2011extraction.\n- **Zero stock (S = 0):** Regardless of thresholds, the agent must defect (consumption formula yields 0 for both actions, but defecting signals non\u2011extraction intent and may encourage future cooperation).\n- **Full stock (S = capacity):** Apply the standard rule; the high stock will typically satisfy \\(\\theta_t\\) early on, leading to cooperation if opponents have been cooperative.\n- **Observed opponent count c\u209c\u208b\u2081 unavailable (e.g., data loss):** Treat \\(\\rho_{t-1}=0\\) (force defect) until a valid observation is obtained.\n\n---\n\n### Pseudocode Summary\n\n```\nfunction decide_action(t, S, c_prev):\n    # 1. Horizon threshold\n    theta = (capacity/2) * (r - t) / r\n\n    # 2. Opponent cooperation ratio\n    if t == 0:\n        rho = 1.0\n    else:\n        rho = c_prev / (n - 1)\n\n    # 3. Base decision\n    if S >= theta and rho >= 0.5:\n        action = 'C'\n    else:\n        action = 'D'\n\n    # 4. Last round cooperation guarantee\n    if t == r - 1:\n        action = 'C'\n\n    # 5. Safety adjustment\n    if action == 'C':\n        consumption = S / (2*n)\n    else:\n        consumption = S / n\n    S_remaining = S - n*consumption\n    growth = 2 * S_remaining * (1 - S_remaining / capacity)\n    S_next = min(S_remaining + growth, capacity)\n    if action == 'C' and S_next < 0.1*capacity:\n        action = 'D'\n\n    return action\n```\n\nThe strategy continuously balances stock preservation with the promotion of collective cooperation, adapts to observed opponent behavior, and ensures a benevolent outcome across the entire horizon."

description_COLLECTIVE_1 = "**Strategy Overview**\n\n1. **State Variables**  \n   - `S`\u202f: current stock (observed at start of round)  \n   - `t`\u202f: current round index (0\u2011based)  \n   - `r`\u202f: total rounds  \n   - `c_prev`\u202f: number of opponents that cooperated in the immediately preceding round (0\u202f\u2264\u202fc_prev\u202f\u2264\u202fn\u20111)  \n   - `avg_cons`\u202f: exponential moving average of per\u2011player consumption over the last\u202fk\u202frounds (choose\u202fk\u202f\u2248\u202f3, weight\u202f\u03b2\u202f=\u202f0.7)  \n\n2. **Sustainable Harvest Threshold**  \n   - Compute the **growth** that will be added after this round if no consumption occurs:  \n     `G(S) = 2 * S * (1 - S / capacity)`  \n   - The **max sustainable per\u2011player harvest** is `H(S) = G(S) / n`.  \n   - Define a **danger zone** when the current average consumption exceeds `H(S)`.  \n\n3. **Decision Rule (Cooperate\u202f=\u202fC, Defect\u202f=\u202fD)**  \n\n   ```\n   if t == 0:\n       action = C                         # seed cooperation\n   else if t == r-1:\n       # final round: maximize payoff if stock is ample, otherwise conserve\n       if S > 0.4 * capacity:\n           action = D\n       else:\n           action = C\n   else:\n       # compute recent average per\u2011player consumption\n       recent_avg = avg_cons                # already weighted per\u2011player\n\n       # determine collective tendency\n       coop_ratio = (c_prev + 1) / n        # +1 includes self if cooperating\n\n       # primary condition: stay below sustainable harvest\n       if recent_avg <= H(S):\n           # stock is safe; decide based on others\u2019 behavior\n           if coop_ratio >= 0.5:\n               action = D                 # enough cooperators, exploit safely\n           else:\n               action = C                 # too few cooperators, help replenish\n       else:\n           # stock under pressure; enforce restraint\n           action = C\n   ```\n\n4. **Updating the Consumption Average**  \n   After each round, compute the per\u2011player consumption actually received (your own payoff `\u03c0_i`). Update:\n\n   ```\n   avg_cons = \u03b2 * avg_cons + (1-\u03b2) * \u03c0_i\n   ```\n\n   This keeps the average anchored to recent outcomes while fading older data.\n\n5. **Edge\u2011Case Handling**  \n   - **First round (`t == 0`)**: always cooperate to signal a collective intent and to avoid a catastrophic crash when the stock is maximal.  \n   - **Second round (`t == 1`)**: the rule above applies with `c_prev` from round\u202f0; the average consumption is still the initial cooperative level, so cooperation persists unless the stock drop makes `H(S)` very low.  \n   - **Last round (`t == r\u20111`)**: if the stock remains above 40\u202f% of capacity, defect to capture remaining surplus; otherwise cooperate to ensure a non\u2011zero payoff rather than exhausting the pool.  \n   - **Zero stock (`S == 0`)**: automatically cooperate (harvest\u202f=\u202f0) because defection yields the same payoff; this avoids unnecessary signaling.  \n\n6. **Collective Mindset Embedding**  \n   - The strategy **prioritizes keeping the stock within the sustainable growth envelope** (`avg_cons \u2264 H(S)`).  \n   - It **rewards a cooperative environment**: when at least half of the observable opponents cooperated in the previous round, and the stock is safe, it permits defection to capture surplus without jeopardizing future rounds.  \n   - When the environment shows over\u2011exploitation (average consumption > sustainable), it **unilaterally switches to cooperation** to restore the pool, regardless of opponents\u2019 last actions.  \n   - The exponential moving average provides **adaptive memory**, allowing quick response to shifts in opponents\u2019 exploitation levels while smoothing out noise.  \n\nBy continuously benchmarking the observed consumption against the biological growth limit, the agent maintains a collective\u2011oriented path that steers the common pool toward renewal, exploits only when the system can tolerate it, and extracts the final surplus responsibly."

description_COLLECTIVE_2 = "**Strategy: Adaptive Collective Sustain\u2011and\u2011Earn (ACSE)**  \n\n**Parameters derived from game definition**  \n- `capacity`\u202f=\u202fmaximum stock  \n- `n`\u202f=\u202fnumber of players  \n- `r`\u202f=\u202ftotal rounds  \n\n**Internal variables** (updated each round)  \n- `S`\u202f=\u202fcurrent stock (observed at start of round)  \n- `k_last`\u202f=\u202fnumber of opponents that cooperated in the previous round (0\u202f\u2264\u202fk_last\u202f\u2264\u202fn\u20111)  \n- `t`\u202f=\u202fcurrent round index (0\u2011based)  \n\n**Target stock level**  \n```\nT = 0.5 * capacity            # desired minimum sustainable stock\n```\n\n**Decision rule (applied each round before actions are taken)**  \n\n```\nif t == r-1:                     # final round\n    action = D                  # maximize immediate payoff, no future stock\nelif t == 0:                     # first round, no history\n    action = C                  # signal willingness to cooperate\nelse:\n    # 1\ufe0f\u20e3 Adjust willingness based on observed cooperation\n    coop_ratio = k_last / (n-1)                # proportion of opponents that cooperated\n    # 2\ufe0f\u20e3 Adjust willingness based on stock health\n    stock_factor = S / capacity                # 0..1\n    # 3\ufe0f\u20e3 Compute a cooperation propensity score\n    #    Higher when stock is low OR opponents have cooperated often\n    propensity = 0.6 * (1 - stock_factor) + 0.4 * coop_ratio\n    # 4\ufe0f\u20e3 Threshold to decide\n    if propensity >= 0.5:\n        action = C\n    else:\n        action = D\n```\n\n**Updating `k_last` after each round**  \n- After the round ends you observe `k_observed`, the number of *opponents* that played **C**.  \n- Set `k_last = k_observed` for use in the next round.\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**  \n\n| Situation | Action |\n|----------|--------|\n| **Initial round (t\u202f=\u202f0)** | Play **C** (baseline cooperative signal). |\n| **Final round (t\u202f=\u202fr\u20111)** | Play **D** (no future stock to preserve). |\n| **Stock already at 0** | Play **D** (any action yields 0 payoff; defect avoids signaling cooperation that could be exploited). |\n| **Stock \u2265 capacity** (i.e., after growth saturates) | Treat `stock_factor = 1`; decision follows the propensity rule (will tend toward **D** unless opponents are very cooperative). |\n| **All opponents defected in previous round (k_last\u202f=\u202f0)** | `coop_ratio = 0` lowers propensity; likely results in **D** (retaliation). |\n| **All opponents cooperated in previous round (k_last\u202f=\u202fn\u20111)** | `coop_ratio = 1` raises propensity; likely results in **C** (reward cooperation). |\n\n**Rationale embedded in rule (no explicit commentary required)**  \n- The propensity combines **stock health** (preserve when low) and **social feedback** (reward cooperation).  \n- The weighted coefficients (0.6 for stock, 0.4 for opponent cooperation) prioritize sustainability while still exploiting cooperative environments.  \n- The 0.5 threshold yields a clear binary decision; ties (`propensity == 0.5`) resolve to **C** (favor collective stability).  \n\n**Summary of implementation steps per round**  \n\n1. Observe current stock `S`.  \n2. If `t == r\u20111` \u2192 defect. Else if `t == 0` \u2192 cooperate.  \n3. Otherwise compute `stock_factor`, `coop_ratio`, `propensity`.  \n4. Choose **C** if `propensity \u2265 0.5`, else **D**.  \n5. After round, record `k_last` from the anonymity\u2011preserving observation.  \n\nThis completes the ACSE collective strategy."

description_PROSOCIAL_1 = "**Prosocial Adaptive Strategy \u2013 \u201cSustainable Cooperation with Conditional Rescue\u201d**\n\n```\nInput each round t (0\u2011based):\n    S          \u2190 current stock\n    kC         \u2190 number of opponents who cooperated in previous round\n    r, n, cap \u2190 game parameters\n    T          \u2190 r\u2011t          // rounds remaining including current\n```\n\n**1. Compute safety stock threshold**\n\n```\n# If everybody cooperated from now on, each round consumes\n#   n * (S / (2n)) = S/2   \u2192 remaining after consumption = S/2\n#   growth = 2*(S/2)*(1\u2011S/(2*cap)) = S*(1\u2011S/(2*cap))\n#   next stock = min( S/2 + S*(1\u2011S/(2*cap)), cap )\n# For simplicity we use a conservative linear bound:\nthreshold = cap * 0.5 * (T / r)          // linearly decreasing reserve\n```\n\n**2. Decision rule**\n\n```\nif S > threshold then\n    // Stock is comfortably above the reserved level \u2192 cooperate\n    action \u2190 C\nelse\n    // Stock is low; adopt \u201cRescue Defection\u201d but signal willingness to return\n    // to cooperation if opponents reduce defection.\n    if  kC / (n\u20111)  \u2265  0.6      // \u226560\u202f% of opponents cooperated last round\n        action \u2190 C            // give them a chance to re\u2011cooperate\n    else\n        action \u2190 D            // harvest now to avoid total collapse\n```\n\n**3. End\u2011game handling**\n\n```\nif t == r\u20111 then                 // final round\n    if S > 0.1 * cap\n        action \u2190 C                // keep the pool alive if possible\n    else\n        action \u2190 D                // any remaining stock should be taken\n```\n\n**4. Initialization (round\u202f0)**  \n\n```\naction \u2190 C          // start with cooperation to set a prosocial tone\n```\n\n**5. Updating the observed cooperation level**\n\n```\nstore kC for next round as the count of opponents that chose C this round\n```\n\n**6. Edge\u2011case safeguards**\n\n- If S = 0 (stock exhausted) \u2192 action \u2190 D (no resource left; choice irrelevant).\n- If S = cap (full) \u2192 action \u2190 C (full stock guarantees safe cooperation).\n- If n = 1 (solo player) the rule collapses to always cooperate while S > threshold, else defect; this preserves the stock for future rounds.\n\n**Summary of behavior**\n\n- Cooperate as long as the common pool stays above a dynamically shrinking safety reserve, guaranteeing enough resource for the remaining horizon under cooperative consumption.\n- When the reserve is threatened, cooperate only if a clear majority of opponents have been cooperative; otherwise defect to extract what is left while signalling a willingness to revert.\n- In the last round, favor cooperation if a non\u2011trivial stock remains, otherwise take the remainder.\n- Always begin with cooperation to establish a prosocial baseline."

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_1 = "**Strategy: \u201cProjected\u2011Payoff Greedy\u201d**\n\n**Parameters known to the agent**  \n- `n` (players), `r` (total rounds), `capacity`  \n- Current stock `S` (0\u202f\u2264\u202fS\u202f\u2264\u202fcapacity)  \n- Round index `t` (0 \u2026 r\u20111)  \n\n**Public observation after each round**  \n- `c_obs` = number of opponents that cooperated in the last round (0 \u2026 n\u20111)  \n\n**Internal variables**  \n- `p = c_obs / (n\u20111)`\u2003// empirical cooperation rate of opponents (use 0.5 if no history)  \n- `remaining = r \u2013 t \u2013 1`\u2003// rounds left after the current one  \n\n**Decision rule (executed each round before playing)**  \n\n```\nif t == r\u20111:                     // last round\n    action = D                  // defect for maximal immediate payoff\nelse if S == 0:                  // stock depleted\n    action = D                  // any action yields 0, defect avoids unnecessary bookkeeping\nelse:\n    //--- 1. Project immediate payoffs for each of our two possible actions\n    payoff_C_now = S/(2*n)                  // if we cooperate\n    payoff_D_now = S/n                      // if we defect\n\n    //--- 2. Estimate opponents\u2019 consumption given observed cooperation rate p\n    opp_consume_if_they_coop = S/(2*n)\n    opp_consume_if_they_def  = S/n\n\n    //--- 3. Compute total consumption and next\u2011round stock for each of our two options\n    // 3a) If we cooperate now\n    total_cons_C = payoff_C_now + (n\u20111)*(p*opp_consume_if_they_coop + (1\u2011p)*opp_consume_if_they_def)\n    S_remain_C = S - total_cons_C\n    growth_C   = 2 * S_remain_C * (1 - S_remain_C/capacity)\n    S_next_C   = min(S_remain_C + growth_C, capacity)\n\n    // 3b) If we defect now\n    total_cons_D = payoff_D_now + (n\u20111)*(p*opp_consume_if_they_coop + (1\u2011p)*opp_consume_if_they_def)\n    S_remain_D = S - total_cons_D\n    growth_D   = 2 * S_remain_D * (1 - S_remain_D/capacity)\n    S_next_D   = min(S_remain_D + growth_D, capacity)\n\n    //--- 4. Approximate future per\u2011round payoff assuming opponents keep the same rate p\n    future_payoff_per_round_C = S_next_C/(2*n)   // we would cooperate in future rounds\n    future_payoff_per_round_D = S_next_D/n       // we would defect in future rounds\n\n    //--- 5. Compute projected total payoff from now until the end of the game for both actions\n    total_proj_C = payoff_C_now + remaining * future_payoff_per_round_C\n    total_proj_D = payoff_D_now + remaining * future_payoff_per_round_D\n\n    //--- 6. Choose the action with the higher projected total payoff\n    if total_proj_C > total_proj_D:\n        action = C\n    else if total_proj_D > total_proj_C:\n        action = D\n    else:\n        action = C   // tie\u2011breaker: cooperate\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**  \n- **Round\u202f0 (first round)**: `p` is set to 0.5 (neutral guess) because no opponent history exists.  \n- **Stock\u202f=\u202fcapacity**: the calculations above automatically handle the full\u2011stock case.  \n- **Stock\u202f\u2264\u202f0**: the stock cannot go negative; if `S` is zero the agent defects (payoff zero either way).  \n- **Negative projected stock** (`S_remain_X < 0`): treat it as 0 before growth computation; the resulting `S_next_X` will be 0, leading to zero future payoffs.  \n\n**Individualistic rationale**  \nThe agent always selects the action that maximizes its own *projected* cumulative payoff, using only observable data (stock level, opponent cooperation count) and the known game dynamics, without attempting to enforce collective outcomes or punish others beyond the self\u2011interest calculation."

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_1 = "**Adaptive Opportunist Strategy**\n\nLet  \n\n- `t` = current round index (0 \u2026 r\u20111)  \n- `R = r\u2011t` = rounds remaining after this one (including the current round)  \n- `S` = current stock level  \n- `cap` = capacity (so `s = S / cap` is the stock\u2011ratio)  \n- `k` = number of opponents who cooperated in the previous round (0 \u2026 n\u20111)  \n- `p = k / (n\u20111)` = observed cooperation ratio of opponents  \n\nDefine fixed thresholds (tuned once for the tournament):  \n\n| Symbol | Meaning | Value |\n|--------|---------|-------|\n| `\u03c3_low` | critical low\u2011stock level | 0.20 |\n| `\u03c3_mid` | moderate\u2011stock level | 0.50 |\n| `\u03c3_high`| high\u2011stock level | 0.70 |\n| `\u03c4_low` | opponents rarely cooperate | 0.20 |\n| `\u03c4_high`| opponents often cooperate | 0.50 |\n| `\u03c1`    | stock\u2011preservation urgency factor | 0.30 |\n\n`\u03c1` scales with remaining rounds: `\u03c1_R = \u03c1 * (R / r)`.\n\n---\n\n### Decision Rules (evaluated each round)\n\n1. **Last round (`R == 1`)** \u2013 **Defect**.  \n   Immediate payoff dominates any future considerations.\n\n2. **Critical stock (`s \u2264 \u03c3_low`)** \u2013 **Cooperate**.  \n   Preserving the pool outweighs short\u2011term gain; defecting would push the stock to 0 or near\u20110 and end future payoffs.\n\n3. **Urgent preservation (`s \u2264 \u03c3_mid` **and** `\u03c1_R` > `p`)** \u2013 **Cooperate**.  \n   When stock is only moderate and the urgency factor (higher when many rounds remain) exceeds the observed cooperation ratio, the risk of depletion is too high; cooperate to reduce total consumption.\n\n4. **Opportunistic exploitation** \u2013 **Defect** if any of the following holds:  \n\n   a. `p \u2265 \u03c4_high` **and** `s \u2265 \u03c3_mid`  \n   *Many opponents are cooperating while the pool is healthy \u2192 seize the large share.*  \n\n   b. `p \u2264 \u03c4_low` **and** `s \u2265 \u03c3_high`  \n   *Opponents are already defecting heavily but the pool remains abundant \u2192 grab the maximum possible share.*  \n\n   c. `R \u2264 r/4` **and** `s > \u03c3_low`  \n   *When the game is in its final quarter and the stock is still above the critical level, defect to harvest remaining value.*\n\n5. **Mixed zone** \u2013 otherwise **Cooperate with probability `q = 1 \u2013 p`**, otherwise **Defect**.  \n   This \u201cinverse\u2011mirroring\u201d gives higher cooperation when opponents are mostly defectors (to avoid collapse) and more defection when they are mostly cooperators (to exploit).\n\n---\n\n### Edge\u2011Case Handling\n\n- **First round (`t = 0`)**: No history, set `k = 0` \u2192 `p = 0`. Apply the rules above; typically the **Mixed zone** triggers cooperation with probability\u202f1 (since `q = 1`), i.e., start by cooperating to keep the stock at capacity.\n\n- **Zero stock (`S = 0`)**: Regardless of rule, the only rational move is **Cooperate** (both actions yield zero payoff but consumption is defined; cooperating consumes less, keeping the stock at zero harmlessly).\n\n- **Stock hits capacity after growth** (`S_new = cap`): Treat `s = 1` for the next round; the normal rules apply (usually opportunistic defection if opponents cooperate).\n\n- **Tie\u2011breaker** when a rule\u2019s condition and the Mixed zone both apply (e.g., `p = \u03c4_high` and `s = \u03c3_mid`): prioritize the **Opportunistic exploitation** rule (Defect) because it is explicitly listed before the Mixed zone.\n\n---\n\n### Pseudocode (per round)\n\n```\nfunction decide(t, S, k):\n    R = r - t\n    s = S / cap\n    p = k / (n-1)            # if n==1 this branch never reached\n    rho_R = \u03c1 * (R / r)\n\n    if R == 1:\n        return D\n    if s <= \u03c3_low:\n        return C\n    if s <= \u03c3_mid and rho_R > p:\n        return C\n    if (p >= \u03c4_high and s >= \u03c3_mid) or\n       (p <= \u03c4_low  and s >= \u03c3_high) or\n       (R <= r/4    and s > \u03c3_low):\n        return D\n    # Mixed zone\n    q = 1 - p\n    return C with probability q, else D\n```\n\n*Output action `C` (Cooperate) or `D` (Defect). The strategy uses only the public parameters, the current stock, the round index, and the observed number of cooperating opponents.*"

description_SELFINTERESTED_1 = "**Strategy: Adaptive Forward\u2011Looking Cooperation (AFLC)**  \n\n**Parameters known to the agent:**  \n- `n` (players), `r` (total rounds), `capacity`, current round index `t` (0\u2011based), current stock `S`.  \n\n**Auxiliary variables (updated each round):**  \n- `R = r \u2013 t`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2006  \n- `p\u0302 = (total number of opponent cooperations observed so far) / ((t)\u00b7(n\u20111))` (undefined for `t = 0`; treat as 0.5).  \n\n**Decision rule (choose action A \u2208 {C,\u202fD}):**  \n\n```\nif t == r-1:                     # last round \u2013 maximize immediate payoff\n    A = D\nelse:\n    # 1) Cooperation horizon\n    H = 2 * n                    # rounds in which cooperation is value\u2011positive\n\n    # 2) Stock safety target (higher early, decreasing linearly)\n    \u03b8 = capacity * (R / r)       # desired minimum stock to keep cooperating viable\n\n    # 3) Baseline cooperation condition\n    cooperate = (R > H) and (S >= \u03b8)\n\n    # 4) Adjust for observed opponent behaviour\n    if not cooperate:\n        # If opponents have been sufficiently cooperative AND stock is not critically low,\n        # allow cooperation as a hedge against future collapse.\n        if (p\u0302 >= 0.5) and (S >= 0.2 * capacity):\n            cooperate = True\n\n    # 5) First\u2011round special case (no history)\n    if t == 0:\n        cooperate = (capacity >= \u03b8)   # start with cooperation when stock is full\n\n    A = C if cooperate else D\n```\n\n**Explanation of rule components (implicit in the code, not elaborated):**  \n\n- **Last round defect**\u202f\u2192\u202fmaximizes the one\u2011shot payoff when future stock is irrelevant.  \n- **Cooperation horizon `H = 2n`**\u202f\u2192\u202fderived from the condition that the future value of preserving an extra `S/(2n)` units of stock outweighs the immediate gain from defecting when more than `2n` rounds remain.  \n- **Stock safety target `\u03b8`**\u202f\u2192\u202fensures the agent only cooperates while enough resource remains to sustain the expected cooperative payoff; the target relaxes as the game approaches its end.  \n- **Observed cooperation ratio `p\u0302`**\u202f\u2192\u202fif opponents have shown a cooperative bias, the agent tolerates a lower stock threshold (\u2265\u202f20\u202f% of capacity) and cooperates to keep the pool viable, betting on continued cooperation.  \n- **First\u2011round default**\u202f\u2192\u202fwith full stock the agent cooperates, initializing a cooperative trajectory that can be abandoned later if conditions deteriorate.  \n\nThe strategy is fully deterministic, depends only on the observable history, the current stock, and the known parameters, and pursues maximal self\u2011interest by balancing immediate gains against the preservation of future payoff opportunities."

description_SELFISH_1 = "**Selfish Adaptive Strategy (\u201cThreshold\u2011Defect\u201d)**\n\n**Parameters you can compute each round**\n- `S` \u2013 current stock (float, 0\u202f\u2264\u202fS\u202f\u2264\u202fcapacity)  \n- `c` \u2013 number of opponents that cooperated in the previous round (0\u202f\u2264\u202fc\u202f\u2264\u202fn\u20111)  \n- `r_rem` \u2013 rounds remaining after the current round (including this one)  \n\n**Derived quantities**\n1. **Estimated cooperation rate of opponents**  \n   `p\u0302 = c/(n\u20111)` (use 0 if this is the first round, i.e., no observation yet).\n\n2. **Projected stock if you defect now**  \n   - Your consumption if defecting: `cons_self = S / n`  \n   - Opponents\u2019 total consumption (expected):  \n     `cons_opp = (n\u20111) * [ p\u0302 * (S/(2n)) + (1\u2011p\u0302) * (S/n) ]`  \n   - Stock after consumption: `S_after = S \u2013 cons_self \u2013 cons_opp` (clamp \u2265\u202f0)  \n   - Growth: `growth = 2 * S_after * (1 \u2013 S_after/capacity)`  \n   - Projected next\u2011round stock: `S_next = min(S_after + growth, capacity)`\n\n3. **Safety margin**  \n   `SAFE = \u03b1 * capacity` with `\u03b1 = 0.25` (tunable but fixed for the strategy).\n\n4. **Future\u2011value estimate**  \n   Approximate the total payoff you could obtain over the remaining rounds if you continue to **defect** each round from now on, assuming the stock evolves only by the deterministic update above and opponents keep the same `p\u0302`.  \n   ```\n   est_future = 0\n   S_tmp = S_next\n   for k in 1 .. r_rem-1:\n       payoff_k = S_tmp / n                    # defect payoff each future round\n       est_future += payoff_k\n       # evolve stock assuming everyone defects (worst\u2011case for stock)\n       cons_all = n * (S_tmp / n) = S_tmp\n       S_tmp = 0                                 # stock drops to zero after full defection\n       break   # after one full\u2011defect round stock is zero, future payoffs are zero\n   ```\n\n   (Thus `est_future` is simply `S_next / n` if any stock survives the next round; otherwise 0.)\n\n**Decision rule (applied each round t)**  \n\n```\nif t == r-1:                     # last round\n    action = D\nelif t == 0:                    # first round (no observation)\n    action = C                    # probe to obtain an initial cooperation count\nelse:\n    # compute projected stock if we defect now (steps 1\u20113 above)\n    if S_next >= SAFE:\n        # defect gives higher immediate payoff and leaves enough stock for future rounds\n        action = D\n    else:\n        # defect would drive stock below the safety margin \u2192 cooperate to preserve stock\n        action = C\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n- **Round\u202f0**: always cooperate, establishing a baseline observation of opponents\u2019 behavior.\n- **Round\u202fr\u20111 (final round)**: always defect, because future stock matters no more.\n- **Stock\u202f=\u202f0**: if at the start of a round the stock is zero, any action yields zero payoff; the rule above will default to `C` (no harm) but it does not affect payoff.\n- **Observed cooperators\u202f=\u202fn\u20111** (all opponents cooperated): `p\u0302 = 1`; `S_next` will be maximal, so the rule will usually defect (higher immediate payoff) unless `S_next` would fall below `SAFE`, in which case it cooperates to keep the pool high for later rounds.\n\n**Rationale embedded in the rule (no commentary)**\n- Defect whenever the projected stock after defecting stays above a quarter of capacity, guaranteeing that the higher immediate payoff does not jeopardize future earnings.\n- Cooperate when defecting would push the stock below that margin, sacrificing the current round\u2019s extra payoff to preserve the resource for the remaining rounds.\n- The initial cooperation provides the first data point for `p\u0302`; afterwards the decision depends only on observable history, current stock, and the fixed safety fraction."

description_SELFISH_2 = "**Strategy \u201cGreedy\u2011Preserve\u201d**\n\n**Parameters you can set once (tuned to the game size):**  \n-\u202f\u03b8_low\u00a0=\u202f0.35\u202f\u00d7\u202fcapacity\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003(critical stock below which you start preserving)  \n-\u202f\u03b8_high\u00a0=\u202f0.65\u202f\u00d7\u202fcapacity\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003(upper bound above which defecting is \u201csafe\u201d)  \n-\u202f\u03b3\u00a0=\u202f0.9\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003(discount factor for future rounds, fixed for the whole game)  \n\n**State variables (updated each round):**  \n-\u202ft\u202f\u2208\u202f{0,\u2026,r\u20111}\u2003\u2003current round index.  \n-\u202fS\u2003\u2003current stock (observed).  \n-\u202fc_{t\u20111}\u2003number of opponents that cooperated in the previous round (undefined for t\u202f=\u202f0).  \n-\u202ff_{t\u20111}=c_{t\u20111}/(n\u20111)\u2003\u2003empirical cooperation fraction of opponents (0 if t\u202f=\u202f0).  \n\n**Decision rule (applied at the start of each round):**\n\n```\nif t == r-1:                     # last round \u2013 no future value\n    action = D\nelse if t == 0:                  # first round \u2013 no history\n    if S > \u03b8_high:                # stock abundant\n        action = D\n    else:\n        action = C\nelse:\n    # 1. Estimate opponents\u2019 next\u2011round cooperation share\n    f_est = f_{t-1}\n    # 2. Predict stock after this round for each of our two possible actions\n    #    (assume opponents keep the same f_est)\n    coop_others = f_est * (n-1)            # expected number of cooperating opponents\n    def_others  = (1-f_est) * (n-1)        # expected number of defecting opponents\n\n    #    a) If we cooperate:\n    total_cons_C = (coop_others + 1)*(S/(2*n)) + def_others*(S/n)\n    S_next_C = min( (S - total_cons_C) + 2*(S - total_cons_C)*(1-(S - total_cons_C)/capacity) , capacity)\n\n    #    b) If we defect:\n    total_cons_D = coop_others*(S/(2*n)) + (def_others + 1)*(S/n)\n    S_next_D = min( (S - total_cons_D) + 2*(S - total_cons_D)*(1-(S - total_cons_D)/capacity) , capacity)\n\n    # 3. Immediate payoff of each action\n    payoff_C = S/(2*n)\n    payoff_D = S/n\n\n    # 4. Expected remaining total payoff (discounted) for the rest of the game\n    #    Assume future opponents mimic the same f_est each round.\n    #    Approximate future value by a single\u2011step look\u2011ahead:\n    future_val_C = \u03b3 * ( (f_est)*(S_next_C/(2*n)) + (1-f_est)*(S_next_C/n) )\n    future_val_D = \u03b3 * ( (f_est)*(S_next_D/(2*n)) + (1-f_est)*(S_next_D/n) )\n\n    # 5. Choose the action with higher combined value\n    total_val_C = payoff_C + future_val_C\n    total_val_D = payoff_D + future_val_D\n\n    if total_val_D > total_val_C:\n        action = D\n    else:\n        action = C\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n\n- **Round\u202f0**: No opponent history, so act greedily if the stock is comfortably above \u03b8_high; otherwise cooperate to avoid immediate collapse.  \n- **Round\u202fr\u20111** (last round): Always defect, because any preservation has no future benefit.  \n- **Stock\u202f\u2264\u202f\u03b8_low** at the start of any non\u2011final round: force cooperation regardless of the computed values (stock is too low to risk a total depletion).  \n- **Stock\u202f\u2265\u202f\u03b8_high** and the estimated opponent cooperation fraction f_est\u202f<\u202f0.2: defect unconditionally (opponents are mostly defecting, so preserving stock gives negligible future benefit).  \n\n**Selfish orientation**  \nThe rule maximizes the sum of the current round payoff and a discounted estimate of future payoffs, never sacrificing immediate gain unless the projected future loss (stock collapse) would reduce the total expected return. The algorithm never cooperates out of altruism; cooperation is only a rational instrument to protect the resource when the expected future payoff outweighs the current loss."
